{"id":"time","duration":62.51,"voice":"Juniper","segments":[{"t":0,"cap":"For time, the first choice is a line or bars."},{"t":3.34,"cap":"A line suits many, evenly spaced time points, when the trend is the story. Bars suit a few separate periods that you compare one by one."},{"t":15.15,"cap":"With only two time points, a line draws a path between them that was never measured."},{"t":20.59,"cap":"Check the spacing of the time axis. When years are skipped but drawn the same distance apart, every slope is bent. Compare the change per year."},{"t":31.82,"cap":"Seasonality is a pattern that repeats every year, like semesters and breaks. To judge growth, compare the same month across years, not neighboring months."},{"t":43.54,"cap":"Calendar plots lay daily values out like a calendar, so day-of-week patterns stand out."},{"t":50.34,"cap":"Finally, animation or small multiples. Animation draws attention, but asks you to remember earlier frames. Small multiples put every time point side by side."}],"items":[{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":0.25,"x":44,"y":30,"h":54,"text":"Lines or bars?","d":0.5,"big":true,"color":"red"},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":3.34,"x":44,"y":84,"h":44,"text":"line: many, evenly spaced","d":0.88},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":7.56,"x":78,"y":128,"h":44,"text":"points, the trend","d":0.6},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":10.52,"x":44,"y":172,"h":44,"text":"bars: a few periods,","d":0.7},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":13.27,"x":78,"y":216,"h":44,"text":"compared one by one","d":0.67},{"k":"sketch","page":0,"t":3.34,"name":"lineMany","box":{"x":500,"y":96,"w":430,"h":414},"phases":[],"end":10.52},{"k":"sketch","page":0,"t":10.52,"name":"barsFew","box":{"x":500,"y":96,"w":430,"h":414},"phases":[],"end":15.15},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":15.15,"x":44,"y":260,"h":44,"text":"two points? the line","d":0.7,"color":"blue"},{"k":"hand","page":0,"t":17.54,"x":78,"y":304,"h":44,"text":"invents the path between","d":0.84,"color":"blue"},{"k":"sketch","page":0,"t":15.15,"name":"twoPoints","box":